      "title": "Lesson 15 | Majaz/ Huruf Al Ma'ani",
      "overview": "In this lesson, we delved into the intricate concepts of \"Haqiqa\" and \"Majaz\" within the context of Islamic jurisprudence. We explored the application of these terms, particularly focusing on how words can carry both literal and metaphorical meanings. The discussion highlighted the importance of understanding the context and customary usage of words to determine whether a literal or metaphorical interpretation is appropriate. We emphasized that when a word can have both a literal and a metaphorical meaning, the literal meaning generally takes precedence unless there is a clear indication or \"Qareena\" suggesting otherwise. This principle is crucial in interpreting religious texts and legal rulings, ensuring that the intended meaning aligns with the speaker's intent and the context in which the words are used.\n\nFurthermore, we examined the role of \"Huroof\" (letters) in conveying meanings, noting that these can also have both literal and metaphorical uses. The lesson underscored the complexity and beauty of the Arabic language, where even small changes in wording can significantly impact the interpretation and application of legal rulings. We discussed how the understanding of these concepts is essential for accurately interpreting religious texts and applying them to contemporary issues.",
