      "overview": "This lesson explores a foundational discussion in Ḥanafī uṣūl al-fiqh concerning the relationship between ḥadīth reports, the legal understanding of narrators, and different levels of qiyās (analogical reasoning). It culminates in the famous legal debate surrounding the ḥadīth of al-muṣarrāh (the artificially unmilked animal), which became a classic case study in how jurists reconcile transmitted reports with established legal principles.\nThe discussion revolves around three major themes:\nThe classification of narrators in Ḥanafī legal theory\nThe distinction between different strengths of qiyās\nThe juristic treatment of a report that appears to conflict with broad legal principles",
      "topic": ""
